# 2. Backup vs. System Restore vs. WinRE

These three concepts have different purposes.

## Backup

**Purpose:** Recover backed-up data or systems.

Example: Restoring a deleted document from an available backup.

## System Restore

**Purpose:** Roll back certain Windows system files, settings, drivers, and installed applications to an earlier state.

Example: Troubleshooting instability that began after a driver installation.

System Restore is not a substitute for a separate backup of personal files.

## Windows Recovery Environment (WinRE)

**Purpose:** Provide recovery tools for certain Windows startup and operating-system problems.

Example: Accessing Startup Repair when Windows cannot start normally.

### Quick Comparison

| Feature | Main purpose |
|---|---|
| Backup | Recover saved data or system information |
| System Restore | Roll back certain system changes |
| WinRE | Access Windows recovery and troubleshooting tools |

### Memory Trick

```text
Backup
  ↓
Recover saved data

System Restore
  ↓
Roll back certain system changes

WinRE
  ↓
Access recovery tools
```

