# 3. Important Windows Recovery Tools

## Startup Repair

Startup Repair attempts to diagnose and fix certain problems that prevent Windows from starting.

Example:

A computer repeatedly fails to boot into Windows.

## System Restore

System Restore returns certain system settings and components to an earlier restore point.

Example:

Windows becomes unstable after a recent driver installation.

## Uninstall Updates

This recovery option can remove certain recent Windows updates when an update is suspected of causing a problem.

Example:

A computer begins experiencing startup problems after a Windows update.

## Safe Mode

Safe Mode starts Windows with a limited set of drivers and services.

It can help troubleshoot problems caused by drivers, applications, or services.

## Reset This PC

Reset this PC reinstalls Windows and offers options affecting personal files and installed applications.

The exact outcome depends on the selected option and Windows configuration.

**Important:** Do not reset or reinstall Windows as your first troubleshooting step. Understand the data risk, check backup availability, and follow organizational authorization procedures.

