# 5. Windows Recovery Decision-Making

| Situation | Appropriate starting point |
|---|---|
| Windows fails to start normally | Investigate the startup failure and consider Startup Repair |
| Problems begin after a driver installation | Investigate the driver and consider System Restore if appropriate |
| Startup problems begin after a Windows update | Investigate the update and consider Uninstall Updates |
| A user accidentally deletes a document | Check the Recycle Bin and available backups |
| Windows is severely damaged | Assess recovery options, data protection, and escalation before resetting |
| A disk may be physically failing | Minimize unnecessary disk activity and escalate for appropriate data-recovery handling |

These are starting points, not guaranteed solutions. Choose an action based on the evidence, device condition, data risk, and organizational procedures.

